hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2690","\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr, informed us Ibn Jurayj, who informed me Abu'z-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abdullah say:\n\n\We used to wear garments when we entered ihram that had not been touched by perfume or saffron. We used to wear al-mumashshaq garments"","" which were nothing but clay.\""\n\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' ibn Kurayb"","" narrated to us Zakariyya ibn 'Adiyy"","" from Ibrahim ibn Humayd"","" narrated to us Hisham ibn 'Urwah"","" from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir"","" from Asma'"","" who said:\n\n\""We used to cover our faces from men"","" and we used to do that before.\"""""""
